<title>UK: RTZ eases despite copper bounce.</title>
<headline>RTZ eases despite copper bounce.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in mining group RTZ Corp stumbled on Monday despite a rise in copper prices.</p>
<p>By 1018 GMT, the shares were off 14-1/2p to 936-1/2p.</p>
<p>Copper prices, meanwhile, bounced on the London Metals Exchange after a smaller-than-expected rise in copper stocks.</p>
<p>But RTZ shares remained weighed down by an overnight drop in CRA, the Australian arm of mining giant RTZ-CRA.</p>
<p>CRA shares lost A$0.160 to A$18.950, the lowest level since mid-October.</p>
<p>&quot;Copper prices were down overnight, and though they're firmer today, they're still net weak,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
